WEBVTT

00:00:00.140 --> 00:00:03.390
بسم الله والصلاة والسلام على رسول الله وعلى آله وصحبه أجمعين 

00:00:03.440 --> 00:00:07.060
Now we begin our study of apparently unrelated aayaat

00:00:07.440 --> 00:00:09.920
and that's not only our first set of case studies

00:00:09.930 --> 00:00:13.400
I'll go through a few of these cases, but before I do,

00:00:13.400 --> 00:00:15.530
just some introductory comments are important.

00:00:15.540 --> 00:00:16.160
Inshallah,

00:00:16.540 --> 00:00:19.610
the first of them is that when you read the Quran,

00:00:19.610 --> 00:00:23.560
it's very clear that sometimes it's not obvious how aayaat are related to each other.

00:00:24.340 --> 00:00:27.620
Things are jumping from a topic that you were expecting

00:00:27.620 --> 00:00:29.540
to a topic that you did not expect at all.

00:00:29.550 --> 00:00:32.159
It will happen and we're going to look at those kinds of cases.

00:00:33.040 --> 00:00:37.390
But this is actually a part of Allah's wisdom, and Allah himself says...

00:00:37.390 --> 00:00:40.390
وَیُعَلِّمُكُم مَّا لَمۡ تَكُونُوا۟ تَعۡلَمُونَ

00:00:40.450 --> 00:00:44.760
He teaches you what you could not possibly have known yourselves.

00:00:45.540 --> 00:00:46.590
Part of that is

00:00:46.810 --> 00:00:49.650
two things that you did not think were connected.

00:00:50.540 --> 00:00:52.850
Only Allah could have known that they're connected.

00:00:53.240 --> 00:00:57.260
Only Allah could have drawn a link between them that teaches you wisdom.

00:00:57.940 --> 00:01:00.460
That's not something you could have discovered yourself.

00:01:00.470 --> 00:01:02.460
That's something only Allah could teach.

00:01:02.840 --> 00:01:04.900
Have you ever been in a class? Sometimes where

00:01:04.900 --> 00:01:07.090
a professor says, "I'm going to talk about something.

00:01:07.090 --> 00:01:10.160
You're not gonna see how it's related to the lesson until the end. Just bear with me."

00:01:10.540 --> 00:01:13.920
He's talking and you're like, "What's he? What's he getting at?"

00:01:13.920 --> 00:01:18.760
What's he getting at? What's he getting at?" And by the end you're like, "Oh, I get it."

00:01:19.140 --> 00:01:23.120
Does that happen? Well, that's the kind of trust you have to have in Allah as a teacher.

00:01:23.130 --> 00:01:25.690
When He switches from one topic to another,

00:01:25.740 --> 00:01:29.360
he's actually pushing you to think, "I put this here on purpose.

00:01:29.840 --> 00:01:31.810
I made this subject change on purpose.

00:01:32.330 --> 00:01:34.370
I want to see what you will find in this.

00:01:35.240 --> 00:01:36.220
To discover this."

00:01:36.840 --> 00:01:41.530
The other way we know for sure aayaat are absolutely related to each other,

00:01:41.680 --> 00:01:43.460
they're absolutely related to each other,

00:01:43.840 --> 00:01:46.260
is from the very beginning of the Quran in the al-Fatihah

00:01:47.040 --> 00:01:48.996
الْحَمْدُ لِلَّهِ رَبِّ الْعَالَمِينَ

00:01:49.019 --> 00:01:50.496
الرَّحْمَٰنِ الرَّحِيمِ

00:01:50.519 --> 00:01:51.676
مَالِكِ يَوْمِ الدِّينِ

00:01:51.706 --> 00:01:52.490
How many aayaat?

00:01:53.440 --> 00:01:54.080
Three ayaat.

00:01:54.080 --> 00:01:56.580
الْحَمْدُ لِلَّهِ رَبِّ الْعَالَمِينَ
is one aayah.

00:01:56.620 --> 00:01:58.670
الرَّحْمَٰنِ الرَّحِيمِ
is two aayaat.


00:01:58.700 --> 00:02:01.330
مَالِكِ يَوْمِ الدِّينِ 
is three aayaat

00:02:01.356 --> 00:02:03.856
But grammatically, how many sentences?

00:02:04.640 --> 00:02:05.800
It's one sentence.

00:02:06.340 --> 00:02:09.990
because the second aayah: الرَّحْمَٰنِ الرَّحِيمِ 

00:02:10.000 --> 00:02:13.570
begins by something that's necessarily connected to what came before.

00:02:13.580 --> 00:02:15.764
Look at:
ٱلرَّحۡمَـٰنُ عَلَّمَ ٱلۡقُرۡءَانَ

00:02:15.790 --> 00:02:16.764
ٱلرَّحۡمَـٰنُ is mubtada.

00:02:16.764 --> 00:02:17.744
عَلَّمَ ٱلۡقُرۡءَانَ is khabr.

00:02:17.790 --> 00:02:18.850
It's one sentence.

00:02:20.040 --> 00:02:24.360
If it's one sentence, in any mind, one sentence is one idea.

00:02:24.940 --> 00:02:25.560
isn't it?

00:02:26.240 --> 00:02:29.520
One sentence is not two ideas. One sentence is one idea.

00:02:29.640 --> 00:02:33.550
And that one sentence is broken up into three aayaat, into two ayaat 

00:02:33.560 --> 00:02:37.060
as if to say three ayaat go together to make how many?

00:02:37.540 --> 00:02:38.260
One idea.

00:02:39.040 --> 00:02:40.860
which means those aayaat are inseparable.

00:02:42.240 --> 00:02:45.210
Allah himself has given us many examples in the Quran

00:02:45.370 --> 00:02:47.660
to let us know that aayaat are inseparable.

00:02:48.740 --> 00:02:49.670
He says...

00:02:49.840 --> 00:02:51.320
فَوَیۡلࣱ لِّلۡمُصَلِّینَ

00:02:52.240 --> 00:02:56.050
"The worst, most terrible, kind of destruction shall fall upon those who pray."

00:02:57.330 --> 00:02:58.050
That's an aayah.

00:02:58.840 --> 00:02:59.650
When Allah (عَزَّ وَجَلَّ)

00:02:59.670 --> 00:03:02.760
says, "The worst destruction shall fall upon those who pray." 

00:03:02.760 --> 00:03:04.500
An aayah by itself.

00:03:04.820 --> 00:03:07.750
It would be pretty bad if you were leading the salah

00:03:08.740 --> 00:03:09.646
and you said...

00:03:09.654 --> 00:03:11.219
أَرَءَیۡتَ ٱلَّذِی یُكَذِّبُ بِٱلدِّینِ

00:03:11.217 --> 00:03:12.799
فَذَ ٰ⁠لِكَ ٱلَّذِی یَدُعُّ ٱلۡیَتِیمَ

00:03:12.796 --> 00:03:14.652
وَلَا یَحُضُّ عَلَىٰ طَعَامِ ٱلۡمِسۡكِینِ 

00:03:14.682 --> 00:03:16.917
فَوَیۡلࣱ لِّلۡمُصَلِّینَ

00:03:16.971 --> 00:03:17.927
أَللهُ أَكْبَر

00:03:22.140 --> 00:03:25.160
"...pushes the orphan. But the worst of them are the ones who pray...

00:03:25.540 --> 00:03:27.460
...Allahu Akbar!"

00:03:29.240 --> 00:03:32.960
You would have to know that that aayah is necessarily connected to what?

00:03:34.040 --> 00:03:35.611
the next aayah. You can't stop the aayah...

00:03:35.611 --> 00:03:37.471
ٱلَّذِینَ هُمۡ عَن صَلَاتِهِمۡ سَاهُونَ 

00:03:37.797 --> 00:03:39.631
فَوَیۡلࣱ لِّلۡمُصَلِّینَ. ٱلَّذِینَ هُمۡ عَن صَلَاتِهِمۡ سَاهُونَ

00:03:39.800 --> 00:03:42.930
The kind of people who pray who are lackadaisical about their prayer,

00:03:42.930 --> 00:03:45.350
who show off when they pray, they are the worst of the worst.

00:03:46.240 --> 00:03:49.660
Okay? The people who have artificial religion are the worst of the worst.

00:03:50.040 --> 00:03:51.560
Okay? So that's

00:03:51.940 --> 00:03:52.740
in and of itself

00:03:52.740 --> 00:03:53.490
by design

00:03:53.490 --> 00:03:56.300
many places in the Quran are teaching us that

00:03:56.300 --> 00:03:58.260
an aayah cannot be looked at in isolation.

00:03:59.540 --> 00:04:03.490
And if that's the case of one or two or three aayaat, it's not for me to say, "Well,

00:04:03.490 --> 00:04:05.510
that's clearly here, but not everywhere.

00:04:06.150 --> 00:04:08.051
I'm going to apply that as a general rule...

00:04:08.028 --> 00:04:09.361
لِیَدَّبَّرُوۤا۟ ءَایَـٰتِهِ

00:04:09.401 --> 00:04:11.650
So they can contemplate His aayaat altogether

00:04:12.040 --> 00:04:13.520
the multiplicity of the aayaat."

00:04:13.530 --> 00:04:16.431
Similarly, you find in Surah Baqarah, Allah says... 

00:04:16.932 --> 00:04:18.901
لَعَلَّكُمۡ تَتَفَكَّرُونَ 

00:04:19.740 --> 00:04:21.560
"So you can think deeply."

00:04:22.440 --> 00:04:23.710
and the next aayah begins with...

00:04:23.718 --> 00:04:25.240
فِی ٱلدُّنۡیَا وَٱلۡـَٔاخِرَةِ

00:04:26.340 --> 00:04:28.493
You can think deeply about what?

00:04:29.140 --> 00:04:30.260
this life and.

00:04:30.480 --> 00:04:32.540
the next life. But it's not one aayaah, it's...

00:04:32.900 --> 00:04:34.390
لَعَلَّكُمۡ تَتَفَكَّرُونَ
is the end of one aayah

00:04:34.780 --> 00:04:36.660
فِی ٱلدُّنۡیَا وَٱلۡـَٔاخِرَةِ
is the next aayah,

00:04:37.240 --> 00:04:38.680
so they're connected to one another.

00:04:38.680 --> 00:04:41.810
These instances in the Quran are already

00:04:41.810 --> 00:04:44.420
screaming at us that there is a necessary,

00:04:44.420 --> 00:04:46.220
necessary connectivity in the Quran.

00:04:46.240 --> 00:04:49.750
Aayaat have to be understood each other. They have to be looked at in flow.

00:04:50.940 --> 00:04:54.660
Sometimes that flow Allah makes all too obvious. Sometimes He needs us to contemplate.

00:04:54.670 --> 00:04:57.980
He wants us to contemplate and reflect and and find it ourselves.

00:04:57.990 --> 00:05:00.560
There is, you know, Muntasir Mir in his book

00:05:01.340 --> 00:05:04.190
He quoted something from the Quran that I wouldn't,

00:05:04.200 --> 00:05:07.460
I'm not as comfortable quoting on the subject, but I'll mention it anyway.

00:05:08.440 --> 00:05:10.860
Uh, he talks about الۡمُقۡتَسِمِینَ

00:05:11.740 --> 00:05:14.020
ٱلۡمُقۡتَسِمِینَ are a group mentioned, I believe, in Surah al-Hijr

00:05:14.470 --> 00:05:15.660
the people who divide up

00:05:16.440 --> 00:05:19.050
The people who divide up. And there was, like 16 opinions.

00:05:19.060 --> 00:05:21.750
Who are these people who divide up?
Because they're critiscising the aayah

00:05:22.440 --> 00:05:23.490
Who are these الۡمُقۡتَسِمِینَ?

00:05:24.240 --> 00:05:27.120
Some said, because اِقتَسَمَ comes from قَسْم

00:05:28.140 --> 00:05:30.560
So these are people who took an oath. They will never accept Islam.

00:05:31.240 --> 00:05:32.450
Maybe it's those people.

00:05:32.460 --> 00:05:35.070
Maybe it's people who swore an oath to one another to

00:05:35.080 --> 00:05:37.660
hold each other to the false religion and not let go.

00:05:38.440 --> 00:05:38.860
Okay,

00:05:40.240 --> 00:05:44.810
the other side said, "No ٱلۡمُقۡتَسِمِینَ is probably those who divided up the religion."

00:05:45.112 --> 00:05:47.612
In other words, this part of the Quran, these pieces I like

00:05:48.012 --> 00:05:50.080
Because قِسْم also means "portion"...

00:05:50.140 --> 00:05:52.460
this portion of the Quran I like, this portion I don't like

00:05:52.570 --> 00:05:55.550
this portion agrees with the Bible, okay, This one doesn't agree with the Bible,

00:05:55.550 --> 00:05:56.160
not okay.

00:05:57.240 --> 00:05:59.760
Others said I like the surah, except this, this, and this part

00:06:00.840 --> 00:06:03.430
they want to do قِسْم of the Quran. تَقسِيم of the Quran.

00:06:03.430 --> 00:06:05.010
That's why they're called الۡمُقۡتَسِمِینَ

00:06:05.070 --> 00:06:08.970
So there were lots of different ways in which the word الۡمُقۡتَسِمِینَ was described.

00:06:08.970 --> 00:06:10.141
But then the next aayah says...

00:06:10.211 --> 00:06:12.711
ٱلَّذِینَ جَعَلُوا۟ ٱلۡقُرۡءَانَ عِضِینَ

00:06:12.840 --> 00:06:15.750
"They took the Quran and they broke it up into portions."

00:06:16.840 --> 00:06:18.800
They took the Quran and broke it into portions.

00:06:18.800 --> 00:06:21.040
Meaning, I'm gonna take this this piece,

00:06:21.050 --> 00:06:22.860
but I don't care about the rest of the pieces.

00:06:23.540 --> 00:06:27.950
And he, actually interestingly, cited it in his book on Coherence in the Quran,

00:06:27.960 --> 00:06:31.740
making the case for it, saying we shouldn't be those who break the Quran into portions

00:06:31.740 --> 00:06:33.760
The reason I'm not comfortable with that argument

00:06:33.770 --> 00:06:35.960
is because the original argument wasn't about this.

00:06:35.970 --> 00:06:38.970
The original argument was about people who want to accept parts

00:06:38.970 --> 00:06:41.260
of the message and not accept other parts of the message.

00:06:42.140 --> 00:06:42.610
Okay?

00:06:42.760 --> 00:06:43.440
in any case,

00:06:43.820 --> 00:06:46.420
now I'm going to share with you some cases of

00:06:46.650 --> 00:06:47.860
apparent

00:06:48.540 --> 00:06:51.130
non existence of coherence in the Quran.

00:06:51.130 --> 00:06:54.931
And the first case study that we're going to look at is Surah Abasa

00:06:57.181 --> 00:06:58.941
This is Surah 80 of the Quran

00:06:59.130 --> 00:07:09.571
And in aayah number 24 to 32 there seems to be a jump in the subject

00:07:09.940 --> 00:07:11.780
in order to help you understand that

00:07:11.790 --> 00:07:12.430
first,

00:07:12.440 --> 00:07:14.420
I'd like you to pay attention as I'm going to

00:07:14.420 --> 00:07:18.040
try to translate in easy language the entire surah,

00:07:18.050 --> 00:07:19.260
because it's a short surah.

00:07:19.640 --> 00:07:23.260
And then I'll highlight the part that seems to be jumping out of subject. Okay?

00:07:24.140 --> 00:07:24.560
So

00:07:24.940 --> 00:07:25.981
عَبَسَ وَتَوَلَّىٰ

00:07:25.980 --> 00:07:27.327
"He frowned and he turned away,"

00:07:27.361 --> 00:07:28.827
أَنْ جَاءَهُ الْأَعْمَىٰ

00:07:28.853 --> 00:07:30.181
"That the blind one came to him."

00:07:30.470 --> 00:07:32.311
وَمَا يُدْرِيكَ لَعَلَّهُ يَزَّكَّىٰ

00:07:32.331 --> 00:07:33.367
"And what would give you any clue."

00:07:33.430 --> 00:07:35.150
Perhaps the blind one that came to him,

00:07:35.160 --> 00:07:38.711
perhaps he wanted to purify himself to become better. 

00:07:38.761 --> 00:07:39.581
أَوْ يَذَّكَّرُ

00:07:39.690 --> 00:07:41.731
"Or he wanted to take some kind of reminder."

00:07:41.800 --> 00:07:42.831
فَتَنْفَعَهُ الذِّكْرَىٰ

00:07:42.869 --> 00:07:44.711
"Thus the reminder will be of benefit to him."

00:07:45.120 --> 00:07:46.105
أَمَّا مَنِ اسْتَغْنَىٰ

00:07:46.105 --> 00:07:48.475
"As for the one who feels like he has no need."

00:07:48.515 --> 00:07:49.955
So to the Prophet (صلى الله عليه وسلم) a blind person came. 

00:07:50.175 --> 00:07:53.070
Abdullah ibn Um Makhtum came. 

00:07:53.080 --> 00:07:55.760
The Prophet (صلى الله عليه وسلم) was kind of upset that he was interrupting a conversation.

00:07:56.340 --> 00:08:00.020
The conversation was being held with the leader of the Quraish. A VIP. 

00:08:00.030 --> 00:08:02.690
So now the next aayaat are going to be about that VIP

00:08:02.700 --> 00:08:03.658
أَمَّا مَنِ اسْتَغْنَىٰ

00:08:03.690 --> 00:08:05.508
"As for the one who feels like he has no need."

00:08:05.705 --> 00:08:06.788
فَأَنْتَ لَهُ تَصَدَّىٰ

00:08:06.820 --> 00:08:08.160
"Then you're leaning towards him."

00:08:08.640 --> 00:08:10.365
You're inclined towards him. 

00:08:10.435 --> 00:08:11.945
وَمَا عَلَيْكَ أَلَّا يَزَّكَّىٰ

00:08:11.995 --> 00:08:14.930
"And it's not your responsibility if he doesn't become a purified person."

00:08:14.940 --> 00:08:16.515
وَأَمَّا مَنْ جَاءَكَ يَسْعَىٰ

00:08:16.490 --> 00:08:18.613
"And as for the one who came to you running,"

00:08:18.713 --> 00:08:19.563
وَهُوَ يَخْشَىٰ

00:08:19.723 --> 00:08:20.963
"And he's full of fear,"

00:08:21.140 --> 00:08:22.450
فَأَنْتَ عَنْهُ تَلَهَّىٰ

00:08:22.473 --> 00:08:25.307
"And you're dismissing him." 

00:08:25.530 --> 00:08:26.860
"You're distracted of him."

00:08:26.870 --> 00:08:29.450
Interestingly enough, he's blind, and yet he's running,

00:08:30.340 --> 00:08:33.330
which is highlighting his desperation to seek some benefit.

00:08:34.120 --> 00:08:38.210
كَلَّا... "No, no,"
 إِنَّهَا تَذْكِرَةٌ... "It is nothing but a powerful reminder."

00:08:38.220 --> 00:08:41.120
It certainly is a powerful reminder.
فَمَنْ شَاءَ ذَكَرَهُ

00:08:41.140 --> 00:08:43.610
"Whoever wants. Then they can make mention of it."

00:08:43.630 --> 00:08:44.940
"They can remember from it"

00:08:45.470 --> 00:08:49.690
فِي صُحُفٍ مُكَرَّمَةٍ...
 "Its origin is in dignified scriptures."

00:08:49.730 --> 00:08:52.820
مَرْفُوعَةٍ مُطَهَّرَةٍ...
"That are elevated and purified."

00:08:52.820 --> 00:08:55.230
بِأَيْدِي سَفَرَةٍ...
"At the hands of noble angels."

00:08:55.310 --> 00:08:58.710
كِرَامٍ بَرَرَةٍ...
"That are dignified and righteous."

00:08:59.040 --> 00:09:03.660
This last part is saying: Why are you desperate to impress this VIP

00:09:03.720 --> 00:09:05.680
with the Quran? The Quran is higher than him.

00:09:06.540 --> 00:09:09.240
The Quran came from the seven heavens.

00:09:09.250 --> 00:09:12.060
He should be honored that he's even getting to hear it.

00:09:12.640 --> 00:09:15.550
So no, it's not at the service of him. He should be at the service of it.

00:09:16.020 --> 00:09:17.890
قُتِلَ الْإِنْسَانُ مَا أَكْفَرَهُ

00:09:18.190 --> 00:09:21.690
May the human being be killed? How ungrateful can he be? Who could that be

00:09:21.690 --> 00:09:22.460
a comment on?

00:09:23.540 --> 00:09:25.660
The leader that's there. How ungrateful are you?

00:09:25.660 --> 00:09:28.550
You're gonna talk like you don't need this message? You're gonna act like that?

00:09:29.440 --> 00:09:31.520
مِنْ أَيِّ شَيْءٍ خَلَقَهُ

00:09:31.580 --> 00:09:33.050
"What was he created from?"

00:09:33.150 --> 00:09:35.260
ٍمِنْ نُطْفَة...
"From a dirty fluid."

00:09:36.440 --> 00:09:37.550
خَلَقَهُ فَقَدَّرَهُ

00:09:37.580 --> 00:09:39.880
"He created him and he put him through stages."

00:09:39.900 --> 00:09:41.330
ثُمَّ السَّبِيلَ يَسَّرَهُ

00:09:41.340 --> 00:09:44.040
"Then he made the pathway easy for him,"

00:09:44.040 --> 00:09:45.860
"The mother opened up and the baby came out."

00:09:46.840 --> 00:09:48.890
Allah is literally reminding that leader of Quraish

00:09:48.920 --> 00:09:50.860
that this is how I started you.

