00:19:29.520 --> 00:19:31.869
لِيُخْرِجَ الَّذِينَ آمَنُوا وَعَمِلُوا الصَّالِحَاتِ

00:19:31.919 --> 00:19:36.290
"So He may take those who believe and do good deeds out from..."

00:19:36.320 --> 00:19:37.380
مِنَ الظُّلُمَاتِ إِلَى النُّورِ

00:19:37.385 --> 00:19:38.900
"...from darknesses into light."

00:19:38.915 --> 00:19:41.010
وَمَنْ يُؤْمِنْ بِاللَّهِ وَيَعْمَلْ صَالِحًا

00:19:41.070 --> 00:19:44.321
"And whoever were to believe in Allah and do good deeds..."

00:19:44.361 --> 00:19:47.970
يُدْخِلْهُ جَنَّاتٍ تَجْرِي مِنْ تَحْتِهَا الْأَنْهَارُ خَالِدِينَ فِيهَا

00:19:47.980 --> 00:19:52.060
"He will enter them into gardens at the bottoms of which rivers are flowing."

00:19:52.070 --> 00:19:53.207
"They will stay in there forever."

00:19:53.207 --> 00:19:54.077
أَبَدًا ۖ

00:19:54.131 --> 00:19:55.567
قَدْ أَحْسَنَ اللَّهُ لَهُ رِزْقًا

00:19:55.587 --> 00:19:59.237
"For such a person, Allah has beautified provisions for them."

00:19:59.290 --> 00:20:01.857
اللَّهُ الَّذِي خَلَقَ سَبْعَ سَمَاوَاتٍ

00:20:01.900 --> 00:20:04.290
"Allah is the one who created seven skies."

00:20:04.350 --> 00:20:05.970
وَمِنَ الْأَرْضِ مِثْلَهُنَّ

00:20:05.970 --> 00:20:08.470
"And of the earth He created seven like them."

00:20:08.490 --> 00:20:10.980
يَتَنَزَّلُ الْأَمْرُ بَيْنَهُنَّ

00:20:10.990 --> 00:20:13.511
"The decision descends from within the seven skies."

00:20:13.626 --> 00:20:14.331
"Through them."

00:20:15.040 --> 00:20:15.706
لِتَعْلَمُوا

00:20:15.716 --> 00:20:17.176
"So that you could know..."

00:20:17.176 --> 00:20:19.456
أَنَّ اللَّهَ عَلَىٰ كُلِّ شَيْءٍ قَدِيرٌ

00:20:19.486 --> 00:20:22.526
"...that Allah is in complete control and capable over all things."

00:20:22.550 --> 00:20:24.316
وَأَنَّ اللَّهَ

00:20:24.316 --> 00:20:25.036
"And that Allah..."

00:20:25.046 --> 00:20:27.196
قَدْ أَحَاطَ بِكُلِّ شَيْءٍ عِلْمًا

00:20:27.246 --> 00:20:30.020
"...has encircled all things with his knowledge."

00:20:30.030 --> 00:20:32.170
All things are encompassed within Allah's knowledge.

00:20:32.640 --> 00:20:34.780
It seems nations being destroyed,

00:20:34.890 --> 00:20:36.430
you better take warning,

00:20:36.690 --> 00:20:38.860
you better take your messenger seriously,

00:20:38.870 --> 00:20:42.340
and Allah sends his command from the seven heavens

00:20:42.550 --> 00:20:44.670
seems completely off topic from what?

00:20:45.550 --> 00:20:46.301
From divorce.

00:20:46.301 --> 00:20:49.741
What are nations being destroyed have to do with divorce?

00:20:49.770 --> 00:20:52.360
They are completely unrelated matters. Or

00:20:52.840 --> 00:20:54.550
are they? That's the issue.

00:20:55.340 --> 00:20:58.370
The most sacred relationship to Allah (عَزَّ وجَلَّ)

00:20:58.500 --> 00:21:01.400
is actually the fundamental relationship he created

00:21:01.400 --> 00:21:04.960
humanity on the basis of. Human beings were created with marriage.

00:21:05.340 --> 00:21:07.350
With Adam (عَلَيهِ الصَلَاةُ وَسَّلَام)

00:21:07.940 --> 00:21:09.920
This is the first relationship.

00:21:09.930 --> 00:21:11.870
It is the foundation of all other relationships

00:21:11.870 --> 00:21:14.540
and how human beings form society and civilization.

00:21:14.550 --> 00:21:18.390
Allah (عَزَّ وجَلَّ) is basically teaching us here that when that most

00:21:18.390 --> 00:21:23.130
personal of relationships is not being regarded sacred,

00:21:23.140 --> 00:21:25.550
the way you come into it and the way you come out of it

00:21:26.240 --> 00:21:31.040
is not being given its sacred due, and that becomes commonplace, then such nations.

00:21:31.040 --> 00:21:34.060
such are the nations that are headed down the path of destruction.

00:21:34.640 --> 00:21:38.840
You would also think, otherwise, that kufr, and shirk

00:21:38.850 --> 00:21:42.140
idol worship, and killing people, and all this other stuff

00:21:42.150 --> 00:21:44.360
when nations did that, they were destroyed.

00:21:45.240 --> 00:21:49.790
But I mean messing around with not giving them mahr or, you know, the iddah,

00:21:49.790 --> 00:21:54.360
or torturing the pregnant wife and not providing for her or whatever else

00:21:54.370 --> 00:21:57.270
come on, that's just a personal thing. It's not like

00:21:57.740 --> 00:22:00.460
it's not like kufr and shirk. Well, according to this surah,

00:22:00.940 --> 00:22:02.260
Allah says, "By the way,

00:22:02.640 --> 00:22:05.150
let me tell you how serious this divorce stuff is.

00:22:05.210 --> 00:22:07.860
Nations were destroyed when they rebelled against Allah.

00:22:08.440 --> 00:22:09.960
Do you understand what I'm saying?

00:22:11.140 --> 00:22:12.850
This is not a small thing.

00:22:13.240 --> 00:22:15.380
This is enough to get entire nations destroyed.

00:22:15.630 --> 00:22:19.060
This will be considered an act of rebellion against Allah, and His messengers

00:22:19.840 --> 00:22:22.060
and people before were very severely punished."

00:22:22.060 --> 00:22:24.250
And then just to get the point across, what does He say?

00:22:24.300 --> 00:22:27.502
فَٱتَّقُوا۟ ٱللَّهَ... which you have read so many times in the Quran.

00:22:27.540 --> 00:22:28.872
"Have taqwa of Allah."

00:22:28.872 --> 00:22:29.962
But he adds...

00:22:29.980 --> 00:22:32.460
فَاتَّقُوا اللَّهَ يَا أُولِي الْأَلْبَابِ

00:22:33.340 --> 00:22:36.550
"Have taqwa of Allah, people of sound minds."

00:22:37.330 --> 00:22:38.560
of clear thought.

00:22:38.940 --> 00:22:41.890
What is Allah compelling people to do in this case?

00:22:42.440 --> 00:22:42.950
Think,

00:22:44.140 --> 00:22:45.850
think why I'm saying this right now.

00:22:46.640 --> 00:22:48.670
Do you realize what I'm getting at?

00:22:49.240 --> 00:22:53.260
You cannot have taqwa of Allah in this case until you connect what's been taught.

00:22:54.140 --> 00:22:56.320
and you can't connect until you apply your minds.

00:22:56.421 --> 00:22:57.330
الَّذِينَ آمَنُوا

00:22:57.330 --> 00:22:57.990
And then He says...

00:22:58.010 --> 00:23:00.860
قَدْ أَنْزَلَ اللَّهُ إِلَيْكُمْ ذِكْرًا

00:23:00.870 --> 00:23:06.370
This is the most remarkable piece. "Allah has certainly sent a reminder to you." Wait,

00:23:06.380 --> 00:23:08.800
Allah said towns were destroyed,

00:23:08.810 --> 00:23:11.960
those who rebelled against the prophets, those who 

00:23:11.984 --> 00:23:13.880
عَتَتْ عَنْ أَمْرِ رَبِّهَا

00:23:13.940 --> 00:23:16.170
previous towns, were those believers or disbelievers?

00:23:17.240 --> 00:23:18.460
Those were disbelievers.

00:23:18.840 --> 00:23:20.330
and usually in the Quran

00:23:20.330 --> 00:23:23.170
when Allah talks about Aad was destroyed, Thamud was destroyed,

00:23:23.170 --> 00:23:24.070
Firaun was destroyed

00:23:24.070 --> 00:23:25.350
Does he talk about them being destroyed?

00:23:26.040 --> 00:23:27.740
Who is he telling to take heed?

00:23:28.720 --> 00:23:29.350
Quraish.

00:23:30.440 --> 00:23:32.580
He's telling Quraish, don't be like Firaun.

00:23:32.730 --> 00:23:34.890
Don't be like Aad. Don't be like Thamud.

00:23:35.540 --> 00:23:39.460
Allah doesn't refer to destroyed nations and say to the Muslims, "By the way, watch out

00:23:39.470 --> 00:23:40.270
I'll destroy you."

00:23:41.240 --> 00:23:42.350
Who does he say that to?

00:23:42.940 --> 00:23:43.960
The disbelievers.

00:23:44.540 --> 00:23:45.460
Don't be like them.

00:23:46.440 --> 00:23:47.760
In this unique surah

00:23:48.340 --> 00:23:51.550
He mentioned previous nations that are destroyed. And who is He Warning?

00:23:52.680 --> 00:24:00.450
فَاتَّقُوا اللَّهَ يَا أُولِي الْأَلْبَابِ الَّذِينَ آمَنُوا ۚ قَدْ أَنْزَلَ اللَّهُ إِلَيْكُمْ ذِكْرًا

00:24:00.540 --> 00:24:06.250
"I'm telling you a reminder. You will not get destroyed by shirk, and kufr, and idol

00:24:06.250 --> 00:24:08.000
worship and disregard of prophets.

00:24:08.010 --> 00:24:12.660
Your destruction will be when you make a mockery of Allah's commandments

00:24:13.740 --> 00:24:17.960
and the place that you should be most careful about is divorce."

00:24:19.290 --> 00:24:22.500
رَسُولًا يَتْلُو عَلَيْكُمْ آيَاتِ اللَّهِ مُبَيِّنَاتٍ

00:24:22.580 --> 00:24:25.230
"A messenger who recites onto you the aayaat of Allah

00:24:25.230 --> 00:24:27.830
making them abundantly clear." Which aayaat are being recited?

00:24:27.830 --> 00:24:30.880
By the way, the word of "رَسُزلًا" in here. Deliberate.

00:24:30.890 --> 00:24:32.080
If you look at the beginning of the surah...

00:24:32.153 --> 00:24:34.520
يَا أَيُّهَا النَّبِيُّ إِذَا طَلَّقْتُمُ النِّسَاءَ

00:24:34.560 --> 00:24:35.600
The Prophet was addressed. 

00:24:35.616 --> 00:24:38.116
Now "ذِكْرًا" replaced with "رَسُوْلًا"

00:24:38.160 --> 00:24:40.080
يَتْلُو عَلَيْكُمْ آيَاتِ اللَّهِ

00:24:40.140 --> 00:24:44.960
Meaning these particular aayaat of Allah are bringing you out of darknesses into light.

00:24:45.540 --> 00:24:47.570
and the good deeds highlighted in this surah,

00:24:47.570 --> 00:24:48.660
generally it's true,

00:24:48.670 --> 00:24:52.360
but specific to the surah are the good deeds of avoiding the wrongdoing of

00:24:52.360 --> 00:24:55.440
the one you're divorcing, or the one being divorced, or the children involved,

00:24:55.440 --> 00:24:56.240
etcetera, etcetera.

00:24:56.250 --> 00:24:56.850
Okay?

00:24:56.850 --> 00:24:59.350
وَمَنْ يُؤْمِنْ بِاللَّهِ وَيَعْمَلْ صَالِحًا

00:24:59.410 --> 00:25:01.690
All of that is all over the Quran. 

00:25:01.750 --> 00:25:03.740
But what addition do you find here that seems deliberate?

00:25:03.776 --> 00:25:06.080
قَدْ أَحْسَنَ اللَّهُ لَهُ رِزْقًا

00:25:06.140 --> 00:25:08.630
"Allah has already beautified rizq for him."

00:25:08.680 --> 00:25:10.370
"For such a person."

00:25:10.440 --> 00:25:13.050
Why is that important? Because when talaq happens, what's divided?

00:25:13.840 --> 00:25:14.350
Rizq.

00:25:15.140 --> 00:25:16.800
There's concern about where it's going to come from,

00:25:16.800 --> 00:25:18.710
Which is why previously in the same surah

00:25:18.740 --> 00:25:22.810
وَمَنْ يَتَّقِ اللَّهَ يَجْعَلْ لَهُ مَخْرَجًا وَيَرْزُقْهُ مِنْ حَيْثُ لَا يَحْتَسِبُ

00:25:23.040 --> 00:25:27.360
So, by the end, Allah gives hope to the one who is thinking they're losing rizq

00:25:27.370 --> 00:25:30.120
That Allah will provide other kinds of rizq. And this doesn't just mean money.

00:25:30.130 --> 00:25:32.960
It means relationships. Who's gonna marry me now? What am I gonna do?

00:25:32.960 --> 00:25:35.790
What am I gonna do? How am I going to raise my kids? Where is the rizq going to come from?

00:25:35.790 --> 00:25:37.940
Not just in terms of, you know, money,

00:25:37.950 --> 00:25:40.490
but also relationships and support and other things.

00:25:40.500 --> 00:25:40.950
Right?

00:25:41.140 --> 00:25:43.770
So Allah gives the hope of better rizq.

00:25:43.940 --> 00:25:45.580
But perhaps the most interesting...

00:25:45.610 --> 00:25:52.240
اللَّهُ الَّذِي خَلَقَ سَبْعَ سَمَاوَاتٍ وَمِنَ الْأَرْضِ مِثْلَهُنَّ يَتَنَزَّلُ الْأَمْرُ بَيْنَهُنَّ

00:25:52.840 --> 00:25:57.460
Have you ever heard before that the decision, like the couples, were made in heaven?

00:25:59.040 --> 00:25:59.350
Right?

00:25:59.350 --> 00:26:04.260
Allah decided that I'm going to marry this person in this country or whatever. And

00:26:04.640 --> 00:26:05.700
you know, when you're not married,

00:26:05.700 --> 00:26:08.390
you're like, "She's looking at the same full moon somewhere.

00:26:08.400 --> 00:26:12.860
I know you're out there. Allah has already made us appear." You know?

00:26:13.740 --> 00:26:17.370
Or, you know, a guy gets married and, like, the first week of his marriage, is like,

00:26:17.370 --> 00:26:19.460
you know, "Allah really does make the pairs, doesn't he?"

00:26:20.140 --> 00:26:22.270
And she's like, "Yes, he does. He does."

00:26:24.050 --> 00:26:24.680
And

00:26:25.140 --> 00:26:27.990
do all marriages last? No, divorce happens.

00:26:27.990 --> 00:26:31.670
And when it happens, either party says, "I thought the pair was made in heaven."

00:26:33.440 --> 00:26:35.210
"Just why am I going through this hell?"

00:26:35.360 --> 00:26:36.950
"If the pair was made in heaven?"

00:26:38.540 --> 00:26:39.370
Allah by the end of Surah

00:26:39.470 --> 00:26:43.660
al-Talaq says the decision comes from the seventh heaven.

00:26:43.660 --> 00:26:46.060
Not only when two people will come together,

00:26:46.640 --> 00:26:48.170
but also when two people will

00:26:48.740 --> 00:26:49.460
come apart. 

00:26:51.040 --> 00:26:52.770
The decision comes from the seven heavens.

00:26:53.540 --> 00:26:57.460
It comes through. And why does it come? And if you're thinking "Well, no, no, no."

00:26:58.240 --> 00:27:04.060
But what? Read the rest of the aayah. So you can know that Allah puts a limit on all things

00:27:06.140 --> 00:27:06.670
قَدْر

00:27:06.820 --> 00:27:09.390
مَنْ قُدِرَ عَلَيْهِ

00:27:09.640 --> 00:27:11.070
Right? To put a limit on all things.

00:27:11.540 --> 00:27:12.610
Some decisions come

00:27:12.610 --> 00:27:16.900
so you're reminded that nothing is forever because Allah puts limits on all things.

00:27:17.740 --> 00:27:19.560
"I thought this was gonna be forever."

00:27:19.940 --> 00:27:20.360
Nope.

00:27:21.140 --> 00:27:22.670
Sometimes Allah decided otherwise

00:27:23.440 --> 00:27:24.570
"And how

00:27:24.710 --> 00:27:25.960
if Allah knew

00:27:26.340 --> 00:27:28.950
Why did He let me get married to this person? If Allah already knew?"

00:27:29.740 --> 00:27:31.170
Questions like that arise.

00:27:31.740 --> 00:27:34.042
This is what the feelings are. And what does Allah say? 

00:27:34.042 --> 00:27:38.802
وَأَنَّ اللَّهَ قَدْ أَحَاطَ بِكُلِّ شَيْءٍ عِلْمًا

00:27:38.840 --> 00:27:41.275
"And Allah has encircled all things in His knowledge"

00:27:41.315 --> 00:27:43.260
Allah knew and you have to go through that experience.

00:27:44.440 --> 00:27:45.520
That was part of your rizq.

00:27:45.680 --> 00:27:48.520
Until a given time. Until the qadr of Allah came,

00:27:48.670 --> 00:27:51.360
the limit came, and the decision descended.

00:27:52.240 --> 00:27:53.670
This was also part of the decree.

00:27:54.540 --> 00:27:56.160
Don't beat yourself up over it,

00:27:56.940 --> 00:27:57.330
okay?

00:27:57.340 --> 00:28:01.260
Gives you a new shade to the meaning of bringing people out of darknesses into light

00:28:01.940 --> 00:28:03.130
in the context of these aayaat. 

00:28:03.200 --> 00:28:07.881
لِيُخْرِجَ الَّذِينَ آمَنُوا وَعَمِلُوا الصَّالِحَاتِ مِنَ الظُّلُمَاتِ إِلَى النُّورِ

00:28:07.940 --> 00:28:09.111
Gives you new meaning to...

00:28:09.111 --> 00:28:11.411
قَدْ أَحْسَنَ اللَّهُ لَهُ رِزْقًا

00:28:11.440 --> 00:28:12.350
The language

00:28:12.360 --> 00:28:15.960
If you looked at these aayaat on their own. If you didn't connect them to Surah al-Talaq.

00:28:16.740 --> 00:28:20.520
If these aayaat belonged to Surah al-Baqarah. If these aayaat belonged to Surah Luqman

00:28:20.530 --> 00:28:23.220
And you read, previous nations were destroyed

00:28:23.230 --> 00:28:26.950
A messenger has come to give you a clear message. Allah has decreed the 

00:28:26.950 --> 00:28:30.450
the decision from the seven heavens. Do these aayaat on their own make complete sense?

00:28:31.240 --> 00:28:32.050
They do.

00:28:32.060 --> 00:28:34.990
But are they teaching an entirely new profound lesson

00:28:35.000 --> 00:28:36.840
in connection with the aayaat of Talaq?

00:28:36.850 --> 00:28:38.260
Yeah, absolutely.

00:28:39.040 --> 00:28:41.207
This is where, you know, he said

00:28:41.240 --> 00:28:44.850
Maulana Hamiduddin Farahi said there are two things that happened with these aayaat.

00:28:44.860 --> 00:28:47.170
There's مَحَاسِن and there's مَنَافِع.

00:28:48.140 --> 00:28:49.460
There's beauty in them.

00:28:50.040 --> 00:28:51.170
And there's benefit in them.

00:28:51.640 --> 00:28:54.550
There's particular benefit for someone experiencing

00:28:54.550 --> 00:28:56.090
When is somebody going to recite Surah al-Talaq?

00:28:57.440 --> 00:28:58.840
When they're going through this crisis?

00:28:58.910 --> 00:29:01.710
They're going to find Allah's guidance in the surah that deals with that crisis.

00:29:01.930 --> 00:29:03.450
And they don't just want to hear,

00:29:03.510 --> 00:29:07.330
 "This is halal, and this is haram, and this is halal and this..." They need hope!

00:29:07.440 --> 00:29:10.290
They need something that will soften their heart because it's a difficult experience.

00:29:10.300 --> 00:29:14.670
So what does Allah do? Allah puts warning, and then he puts hope by the end.